    <div class=3D"flex flex-col w-1/2 justify-center">
        <h2 class=3D"mb-8 text-2xl font-bold">About</h2>
        <p class=3D"text-justify">
            The CREA III project builds on the success of the previous CREA=
 project (2017-2019). Its main goal is to use Artificial Intelligence (AI) =
to help people and organizations resolve disputes. By using advanced AI too=
ls and game theory algorithms, CREA III will offer a new way to settle conf=
licts.
            <br>
            <br>
            The CREA III project leverages advanced Artificial Intelligence=
 (AI) and game theory algorithms to assist individuals and organizations in=
 resolving disputes more effectively. Building on the success of its predec=
essor, CREA (2017-2019), CREA III introduces innovative solutions to stream=
line the dispute resolution process.<br>
            <br>
        </p>
        <p class=3D"font-bold text-center my-16">
            Our mission :<br>
            Enhance access to Online Dispute Resolution (ODR) tools, breaki=
ng down barriers to justice and enabling more efficient and equitable confl=
ict resolution
        </p>
        <p class=3D"text-justify">
            Key novelties of CREA III :<br>
            <br>
            </p><ul class=3D"project-list">
                <li>
                    <span class=3D"font-bold">AI-powered dispute resolution=
:</span> Advanced AI and machine learning help deliver faster and more prec=
ise legal solutions.<br>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class=3D"font-bold">Smart contracts with Blockcha=
in:</span> Legally binding agreements are created using secure, decentraliz=
ed Blockchain technology.<br>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class=3D"font-bold">European Common Ground of Rig=
hts (ECGAR):</span> This system bridges the gaps between different legal sy=
stems, working with common legal rights across EU countries.<br>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <br>
            The EU users will have access to all the functionalities of thi=
s novel approach through a user-friendly Web Interface.<br>
            <br>
            The project Consortium will also organize 3 workshops =E2=80=93=
 one per planned work =E2=80=93 and 5 seminars in every partner=E2=80=99s M=
S to provide a platform that fosters discussions, exchange and spread of kn=
owledge about these new algorithms through several AI tools and ECGARs. In =
turn, the results thereof will feed into the work of the project.  The proj=
ect will involve =E2=80=93 as main target groups =E2=80=93 a wide range of =
EU stakeholders, including over 150 lawyers, 30 notaries, 50 mediators, 5 c=
onsumer associations, 100 academics, 300 students, 5 legal tech companies, =
5 policy makers.
        <p></p>
